	(layer "F.Cu")
	(descr "PCI Express Mini Card socket, 52 positions at 0.8 mm, SMT, 4.0 mm height (TE 2041119-1/-2 type I, Molex 67910-0002 class) with the two M2.5 standoff holes of a full-size 30 x 50.95 card. Land pattern from TE Connectivity customer drawing C-2041119 rev D, 01JUN16, sheet 2 (recommended PC board pattern layout for full card connector, detail D): pads 0.6 x 2.0 in two rows 3.1 either side of the locating-hole line; odd row (pin 1 side, socket rear) pin 1 at 0.7 and pin 17 at 10.3 right of the dia 1.6 hole, even row (card side) pin 2 at 1.1 and pin 18 at 10.7, key gap 4.0 between pins 15/17 and 16/18, end tabs 2.3 x 3.2 centred 3.5 rear of the hole line and 2.15 outside each locating hole, locating holes dia 1.6 and dia 1.1 25.0 apart, housing 29.9 x 8.2 (sheet 1) 4.6 on the card side and 3.6 on the rear of the hole line. Card from sheet 3 and Quectel EG25-G Mini PCIe Hardware Design V1.0 fig. 19: 30 +0/-0.3 x 50.95 +0/-0.3, holes dia 2.6 25.7 +/-0.15 apart, 2.15 from the side edges and 48.05 (DIM F) from the contact edge, key slot 1.5 wide centred 8.65 right of the dia 1.6 hole (2.35 from pin 15, 1.65 from pin 17), tongue 25.7 wide over the first 3.2 mm, card centreline 12.5 right of the dia 1.6 hole. Standoff holes dia 2.7 NPTH on 25.7 x 48.05 with a 6.3 courtyard each (TE sheet 2 keeps a 5.8 square free for the hold-down). Origin: card centreline x, locating-hole line y; the card extends toward -y with its contact edge on the hole line; pin 1 at -11.8, +3.1. Sources: https://www.te.com/commerce/DocumentDelivery/DDEController?Action=showdoc&DocId=Customer+Drawing%7F2041119%7FA%7Fpdf%7FEnglish%7FENG_CD_2041119_A.pdf%7F2041119-1 (vendor/lte/te-2041119-mini-pcie-msata-socket-4mm-customer-drawing-rev-d.pdf); vendor/lte/quectel-eg25-g-mini-pcie-hardware-design-v1.0.pdf")
	(tags "mini pcie socket 52 0.8mm H4.0 standoff")
